WEBVTT

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.130
My mother went to Jingu Music School

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.550
and her lifelong dream was to create
another school in that same location.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.430
So that's why she established Yuigaoka...

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.890
But my father was assigned to work
overseas and was against this idea

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.020
and left us.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.060
Even then, my mother worked hard
until the school was finished...

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.440
Part of the reason was overwork,
but she passed away two years ago.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.490
So when you said you're alone...

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.410
Yes.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.370
And that you didn't have any money?

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.620
It's embarrassing to admit, but yes.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.290
My father offered to let me live with him
overseas, but I turned him down.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:49.630
I want to make the school that my mother
left me the best in this whole city.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:54.880
If I don't gather even more students,
I cannot accomplish this goal.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.930
Sorry for barging in on you.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:01.890
It's all right.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.230
Looking back at how I'd
been acting... I can't blame you.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.600
Hazuki-<i>san</i>...

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.980
Um...

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.520
Regarding everything
I've told you today...

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.780
Could you please keep it between us?

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.070
But...

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.110
I don't want to make the students anxious

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.450
or feel like they regret
coming to Yuigaoka.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.330
Please.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.250
Mother.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.090
What were you trying to tell me back then?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:40.220
<i>You can't stop real dreams</i>

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:45.890
<i>Our hearts are about to start running</i>

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.150
"Love Live! Superstar!!"

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:07.000
<i>Before we knew it,</i>
<i>we found something that we loved</i>

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.500
<i>Let these feelings reach you</i>

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.170
<i>We've made up our minds, we're serious!</i>

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.960
<i>I wonder what we can do</i>

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.880
<i>The sky's so bright</i>

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:23.300
<i>Let's look up at it</i>
<i>and sing our hearts out</i>

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.390
<i>Doesn't having something you want to do</i>

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.060
<i>Make every day fun?</i>

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.150
<i>Do you feel that way, too?</i>

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.440
<i>Ah, we've been waiting for this moment</i>

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.490
<i>This encounter is where we start</i>

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:45.870
<i>Our dreams are drawn together,</i>
<i>and it all begins</i>

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:51.670
<i>We realized our true desires and now,</i>
<i>we can't be stopped</i>

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:57.050
<i>Our hearts are about to start running</i>

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:02.890
<i>As fast as they can run</i>

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.180
So the reason she wanted to
conduct the school festival

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.560
with just the music program...

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.440
Is probably because there weren't
that many new applicants for the school.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:16.150
And the efficient music program
would be able to attract people.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.650
So it's her last resort.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.650
Ow!

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.900
This is why people care less
about the general curriculum!

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.320
--Shut up!
--I can understand where
she's coming from,

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.490
but no one else knows her situation.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.790
Yeah.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.250
But... At this rate, Hazuki-<i>san</i>...

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:34.290
Everyone will continue to have
the wrong idea about her.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.130
Hazuki-<i>san</i>.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.340
"Signatures opposing the school festival"

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.050
Here are signatures we collected
protesting the school festival.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.890
Just because you're the founder's daughter

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.800
doesn't mean the school belongs to you.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.390
Please think about this!

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.140
Please take this up with
the student council.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.980
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.400
What's with that attitude?

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.190
She's unbelievable!

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:02.070
I'll try to go talk things out.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:05.370
This is the only time it'll
concentrate on the music program!

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.370
It's not like we're saying
that you can't be involved at all!

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.410
They're more confrontational
than I thought they'd be.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.960
Clearly, it's the general curriculum kids
who are being selfish here!

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.630
Don't let them overwhelm you like that!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.500
Well...

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.130
We don't want to participate.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:25.260
Participating is like the music program
saying, "Oh, we'll let you help out."

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.800
I wouldn't go that far...

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.600
I think it's a good idea
to have the festival

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.230
showcase music since
it represents our school...

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.400
Then why didn't they ask us
to participate to begin with?

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.400
Like she said in her campaign promise!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.150
Why are you taking the student council
president's side anyway?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:47.660
Yeah! She's going to say no if you say
you want to perform at the festival!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:50.410
You dummy. Quit repeating the same things.

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:53.290
Okay, then you say something, Sumire-<i>chan</i>!

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.790
Don't you want to continue being
a school idol, Shibuya-<i>san</i>?

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:59.670
We've been rooting for you!

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.880
Actually, they're right.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.590
Hazuki-<i>san </i>is against school idols.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.720
I'm going to take the side
of the general curriculum!

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.430
Let us fight together!

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.470
Yeah!

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.890
Stop making things more complicated!

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:18.060
♬ Someday, I can fly ♬

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.320
♬ Someday, I can... ♬

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.530
They just keep going.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:27.240
Looks like they don't care
about the rest of us.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.490
At this rate, Hazuki-<i>san </i>will be...

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.950
I hate her.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:35.290
We go to Yuigaoka, too!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.460
What should we do?

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.960
Things are getting even more complicated.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:46.800
Well, yeah. Everyone's always felt
this divide between the two programs.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.510
Yes, and it doesn't look like
either side will back down.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.430
Yeah...

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.220
This is all my fault.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.520
Hazuki-<i>san</i>!

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.770
One of the music program students told me
that you went to talk to them.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:05.190
Yeah. We thought we might be able to help.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:09.990
Don't worry! We haven't mentioned
anything about your private life.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:15.910
I'm truly sorry. My words
have now troubled everyone.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.420
You mean you regret what you said?

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:23.840
Yes. The director summoned me
to her office earlier.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.340
You need to clear things up
tomorrow at the assembly.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.970
If you fail to come to a solution,

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:32.600
this year's school festival
will be canceled.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.720
But...

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.350
The director went to school
with my mother,

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.810
but she seems rather conflicted about me.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.520
We still have some time!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.650
Let's just talk with both programs
and do something together!

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.990
There's something else on your mind?

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:54.160
Yeah. I think we can make this work
if you talk to everyone at the assembly.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.660
Of course, I would love to do that.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:59.500
It's just, school idols are...

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.380
Just anything other than
school idols, please!

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:09.880
I'd rather you didn't do
idol activities at this school.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.430
Will you tell us why?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:19.680
This school once had students
who performed as idols

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.190
to save it from closing.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:26.150
One of them was my mother.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:30.110
So that's why this room had
the school idol club plate on the door.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:34.070
This is long before they were
officially referred to as "school idols."

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.330
Their performances
became rather popular

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.240
and they gathered a lot of attention.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.750
But they weren't able to reach their goal
and the school closed.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.420
That's why I thought
I would become a school idol

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.260
at this school that my mother founded.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:54.140
I thought I would get attention for
the school just like my mother did.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:57.760
But you were so against us doing it!

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.350
But...

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.890
Then let's do this together!

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.480
If we all work together, we--

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:06.150
There's just nothing left!

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:08.070
No matter how hard I looked...

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:14.280
...I couldn't find any record
of her school idol activities.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:18.790
Even though there were records
of every other school activity...

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:23.790
There is no record of her ever doing
idol activities at the school.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:29.050
And that made me wonder...
Did my mother regret being an idol?

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.930
Did she feel like she couldn't
save the school as a school idol?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.140
But...

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.470
But that's not set in stone!

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:39.930
Then why does nothing exist?

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:43.350
She didn't leave a single photo of
these supposed precious memories.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.060
How is that possible?!

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:48.570
What do you think?

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:51.190
I can understand how she feels,

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:56.740
but I think it's going too far
to prohibit school idols!

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:01.660
I mean, in the end,
this doesn't concern us.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.160
What about you, Kanon-<i>chan</i>?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:09.960
I really can't imagine her mother
regretting her school idol activities.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.470
I saw a picture of Hazuki-<i>san</i>'s mom
smiling at their house

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.130
and it was dazzling.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.640
I want to find out for sure.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.100
Records from the Jingu Music School?

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:27.850
Yes. I'd like to see anything
you might have on file.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.860
Please.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.070
The school assembly will be starting soon.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.860
I promise we'll return them by then.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.450
Make sure you don't make a mess.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:39.820
This isn't it.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:41.030
This isn't either.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.200
There are records of
all the other club activities

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.210
except for any school idol activities.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.870
There's nothing over here, either.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.790
I've looked through everything many times.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:51.630
Hazuki-<i>san</i>.

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.880
That's the only thing missing.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.880
I can only imagine that
she willingly got rid of them.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.930
She never said anything?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:03.350
No... She may have mentioned
something when I was little...

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:05.980
Though she would always say,

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:10.440
"I hope our feelings connect
in the same place."

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.820
The same place?

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:15.530
That's why she made
the school here, right?

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:20.490
The school assembly is
about to start. I must go.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.030
What are you going to do?

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:25.160
I'll probably have to
talk to everyone honestly

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.370
about the current state of this school.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.960
Though I'm uncertain
how that will turn out.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:35.340
Feelings connecting in the same place...

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.880
Wait!

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:42.760
Hazuki-<i>san</i>. You gave us the key
to this room, right?

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.850
Oh. The director said
she couldn't find them,

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:49.480
so when I looked around my house,
I found them in my desk...

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.360
Shibuya-<i>san</i>! No running in the hallway!

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.770
"School Idol Club"

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.770
Shibuya-<i>san</i>! No running in the hallway!

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.980
Kanon-<i>chan</i>!

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.740
What did we see when
we first came to this room?

00:10:58.740 --> 00:10:59.860
I can't really remember.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.360
It's in here?

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.740
I'm not sure. But I think
we'll find something!

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:08.290
I didn't see anything over here.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.330
It's just storage.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.380
Something... There has to
be something here!

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.850
Wait... I think this is it!

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:28.020
<i>Love Live! Superstar!!</i>

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:32.900
We will now begin our school assembly.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.690
First, the student council
president would like to

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:38.650
say a few words regarding
the school festival.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:43.570
I am the student council
president, Ren Hazuki.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.740
Before I speak about the school festival,

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:48.830
please allow me to apologize to you
for my remarks the other day

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:52.620
and the confusion they have caused.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:54.880
I'm truly sorry.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.880
I'm sure that many of you
felt unpleasant or angry.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:02.720
It's just that I want people on the
outside to see how wonderful this sch--

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.220
What's going to happen
to the general curriculum?

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.060
Are we going to be able to
participate in the school festival?

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:08.720
Um...

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.810
We want to sing even if
we're not in the music program!

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.640
Do we even get that chance?!

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.060
Just having us as helpers
to the music program is cruel!

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:17.570
Please take back what you said!

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.610
Are you going to prohibit
school idol activities, too?

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.610
They've done more for
this school than anyone else!

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:26.570
That's the only thing I...

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:27.870
Wait!

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:34.750
Kanon-<i>chan</i>?

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.010
Hazuki-<i>san</i>, there's something
I'd like to say.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.220
Shibuya-<i>san</i>.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.180
Very well.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.590
Please go up to the stage.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.730
They're all looking at me...

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.110
"Jingu Music School"
"Idol Club Diary"

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:02.780
What is that?

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:09.030
We found this notebook
in the school idol club room.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.990
This is something the students from

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:15.670
the Jingu Music School wrote
before this school was created.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:19.460
These students tried to gather
students to do idol activities

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:23.170
when they learned that
the school was going to close.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:28.090
This is what was written inside.

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:34.350
"We continued being idols at our school,
but we're still going to lose our school."

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:37.150
"We couldn't stop
our school from closing."

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:46.860
"But we don't regret anything we've done."

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:47.990
"Jingu Music School"
"Idol Club Diary"

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.870
"The Jingu Music School
Idol Club Begins!!"

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.580
"Because we came together as a school."

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:58.540
"Through our activities, through music,

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.290
we all connected!"

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:04.840
"We were able to make
the best school ever!"

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.130
Mother...

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.220
"We all worked together,
dreamed the same dream,

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.390
and went through all kinds
of emotions together."

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:17.600
"This time we spent together
was like a miracle."

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:21.230
"And that's why I promised everyone..."

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:26.990
"That I would create a school that has
'connect' in the name here once again."

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:27.490
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School"

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:27.490
"That I would create a school that has
'connect' in the name here once again."

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:29.660
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School"

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:29.660
"I'm going to create a school
that connect everyone

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.240
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School"

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.240
through music here once again."

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:37.040
"That is my dream.
My dream I will see come true."

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:45.630
Your mother created this school and wanted
to connect everyone through music.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:49.720
This school is to make
that dream come true.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:53.680
A school where the students of
both programs can be connected.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:02.810
Being a school idol was
your mother's best memories.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:08.280
Her best... memories...

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:12.700
Ren, being a school idol...

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:19.080
...were my best memories.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:27.670
This was tucked away with the notebook.

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:31.180
Mother...

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.390
Mother...

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:40.440
Mother!

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.570
Upsy daisy.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:50.650
Here you go. All that's left
of your mother's activities.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:56.830
You knew, didn't you?
That my mother was a school idol.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:16:00.410
Well, yes. Though I was
on the supporting side.

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:02.710
Why didn't you tell me?

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:06.290
Don't be too harsh with me, will ya?
She asked me not to say anything.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:10.760
She wanted you to make your own decisions
and for me to watch over you.

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:13.220
Honestly, talk about a pain.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:14.340
By the way...

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:15.720
Why are you speaking differently?

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.890
Hey, this is how I usually am.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.310
Well, you understand now,
so get a move on!

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.850
Get ready for the school festival!

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:24.400
Yes, ma'am! Please excuse us.

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.400
I'm sorry.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:33.820
We're rather behind on the school festival
preparations because of me.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:36.280
Come with me.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.450
Wow...

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:38.740
A little more to the right.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:39.830
Like this?

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:40.700
Yeah!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.040
Where's the stepladder?

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:45.250
--Got it! Here you go!
--This is the school idols'...?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:50.050
Yup. The stage we're all creating for
our performance for the school festival.

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:51.920
All...

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.840
Say, Hazuki-<i>san</i>.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:08.060
Hazuki-<i>san</i>... No, Ren-<i>chan</i>.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:11.740
Won't you be a school idol with us?

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:20.290
I have no right to do that
after all the grief I caused you...

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:24.410
I want to sing with you
as a school idol, Ren-<i>chan</i>.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.080
For the sake of this school... No.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.630
For the sake of all of the feelings
created in this place.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:45.480
Don't worry! You can do it!

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.020
Be more honest with yourself.

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:50.110
We're always fine, fine!

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:26.350
Okay! Let's all get ready
for the school festival!

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:28.230
Yeah!

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:31.820
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School 1st
School Festival!"

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:31.820
Our first ever school festival
is next Sunday!

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.610
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School 1st
School Festival!"

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.610
We'll be selling some rainbow <i>takoyaki</i>!

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.900
We hope you'll come support us!

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.570
Huh. I guess they're doing
a school festival.

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:40.700
Looks like it.

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:44.540
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.080
One, two, three...

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.000
Amazing, Ren Ren!

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:53.380
Your figure skater skills are paying off!
You're nothing like that giant isopod.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.920
I keep telling you
to stop calling me that!

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.050
I'm happy.

00:18:57.050 --> 00:19:00.640
You just joined but you're
basically fit to lead us.

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.720
You're far too kind.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:06.270
Ren-<i>chan</i>, want to try being the center?

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:09.020
It's going to be this school's
first school festival.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.190
Yes, but...

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:14.570
And I want you to sing, Ren-<i>chan</i>.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.400
Me, too.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.070
Me, three.

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:23.200
Well, I'm only going to be the center
on a much bigger stage.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.660
Guess it's settled.

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:26.950
Coming through!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:27.250
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School 1st
School Festival!"

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:27.250
Coming through!

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.870
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School 1st
School Festival!"

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.870
Looking good!

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:31.000
Okay, over here next!

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.540
Everyone's staying this late?

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.710
We all want everyone to notice our school.

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:40.470
Everyone said we're
going to help create it together.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:44.140
Do you think we'll get more applicants?

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.350
To be honest, I have no idea.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:49.980
But we just have to do this.
We just have to believe.

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.650
You're quite strong,
aren't you, Kanon-<i>san</i>?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:58.900
I wouldn't say that. It's just...
I love the moment something begins.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.360
Oh, I know!

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.620
What is this?

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:07.080
Since we're all here,
I figured we could try it.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:11.710
Could it be? I'll do it!
I've always dreamed of this!

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:13.880
Can't we just do the usual "hey" thing?

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.000
Well, we're school idols.

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:20.670
Let's connect this school through music!

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:24.800
One!

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:25.760
Two!

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:26.550
Three!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:27.220
Four!

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:28.850
Five!

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:32.020
Yuigaoka Girls' High School Idol Club!

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.440
--Song for me! Song for you!

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:34.940
--♬ (Sing along with me ha-a) ♬
--Song for me! Song for you!

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.230
--♬ (Sing along with me ha-a) ♬
--Song for all!

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:43.820
♬ I felt this on the day that we met ♬

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:47.620
♬ My desire to make this come true
just keeps growing (Starting day a-) ♬

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:48.580
"Yuigaoka Girls' High School 1st
School Festival!"

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:48.580
♬ My desire to make this come true
just keeps growing (Starting day a-) ♬

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.250
♬ My desire to make this come true
just keeps growing (Starting day a-) ♬

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:57.750
♬ I'll help you protect the thing
you held onto so tightly ♬

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:04.380
♬ That you were shaking because
you didn't want it to disappear ♬

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:12.270
♬ Even the morning sun's bright rays
or sudden showers ♬

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:21.990
♬ Become irreplaceable moments when
I'm able to smile together with you ♬

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:29.120
♬ Those passionate feelings
within your chest ♬

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:31.450
♬ On this staff notation ♬

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:36.420
♬ Let's weave them together and
make them resonate through the blue sky ♬

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:42.960
♬ Tears just don't suit you anymore ♬

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:49.930
♬ Let's all go together
and keep on believing ♬

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:58.230
♬ This Wish-Song always gives us courage ♬

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:12.040
♬ The melody of hope
that we heard back then ♬

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:17.540
♬ Created this wonderful present ♬

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:24.550
♬ Let's hold it tight
and take it with us ♬

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:28.260
♬ On this staff notation ♬

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:35.560
♬ The future we wove together
is overflowing with light ♬

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:42.070
♬ A smile always looks the best on you ♬

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:49.070
♬ Let's all go together
and keep on believing ♬

00:22:49.070 --> 00:22:57.460
♬ This Wish-Song always gives us courage ♬

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:26.440
Thank you so much!

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:30.110
We're Yuigaoka Girls' High School's...

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:34.780
...school idols!

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:41.040
"Connected Feelings"

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:46.550
Next time, "What's Your Name?"
